.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-status 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-status \- Show UPS status
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut status\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-ups\fR] [\fB\-\-upsd\-address\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-upsd\-port\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show UPS status
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Color when writing to a terminal (default)
.IP \(bu 2
always: Color even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never color
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
Continuously refresh the status view
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Include raw NUT variables
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-\-ups\fR \fI<UPS>\fR
UPS name (defaults to the selected host configuration, or `primary`)
.TP
\fB\-\-upsd\-address\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
Loopback upsd address (defaults to host configuration, or 127.0.0.1)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-\-upsd\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Loopback upsd port (defaults to host configuration, or 3493)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
